            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0217" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1967: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-03T13:00:00+08:00">October 3, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 3—2:54 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s telegram of October 2nd [, 10 a.m.]<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d112-f1"/> Radio station held by Japanese authorities who report it
                    undamaged. Repeated representations to Japanese Consulate relative to
                    reestablishment of service fail to elicit more than statement that the Japanese
                    authorities are considering the matter. Only facility for communication outward
                    is the Japanese telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
